Subject: Cantor Identity Admission Journal Transport P5 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 1268a1e7-bd44-4015-97e4-b52f093b6e4d

& [Why]
  + P4 proves admission eligibility but intentionally returns only an in-memory successor
  + P1 and P2 already provide exact event replay snapshot persistence mutex serialization and MCP custody

& [WhyThisShape]
  + one new tagged operation reuses every proven layer and retains the complete Judgment record as event evidence
  + schema derivation is mechanical exposure, not a new faculty behavior

& [Rejected]
  + direct MCP insertion because it bypasses P4
  + opaque admission JSON because it weakens schema and substitution checks
  + separate service because it forks custody and compare-and-set authority
